From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Portal <116828772+Retrorerr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not repaint the output for a consumed repaint request

RenderLayer::scheduleRepaint(Item *) marks the layer as needing a
repaint, but Compositor::prePaintPass() cleared that mark only when the
layer also had a repaint region of its own. The scene layer collects
item repaints through its delegate and has no region, so once any item
repainted, the mark stayed set and every later frame request rendered
the whole scene. Anland requests a frame for every buffer the consumer
selects, so each touch made KWin render and the consumer present about
180 identical frames. Clear the mark once a frame has served it.

A frame can still have nothing new when a client only asked for a frame
callback. The Anland layer now reports such a frame as skipped, so the
consumer keeps showing the identical frame it already presents.
---
 src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 src/compositor.cpp                         | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
index dc0917f..5b063d7 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_egl_backend.cpp
@@ -227,6 +227,15 @@ bool AnlandEglLayer::doEndFrame(const QRegion &renderedDeviceRegion, const QRegi
         m_accumDamage[i] = m_accumDamage[i] + damagedDeviceRegion;
     m_accumDamage[m_currentIndex] = QRegion();
 
+    if (damagedDeviceRegion.isEmpty()) {
+        // Nothing changed since the last rendered frame (a client asked only
+        // for a frame callback), and that frame is the one the consumer
+        // shows: report this one as skipped rather than present a copy. The
+        // repaint owed by this buffer is done either way.
+        discard_render_fence(m_display);
+        return true;
+    }
+
     // Instead of CPU-blocking on glFinish, create a fence for the just-submitted
     // GPU work and hand it to the consumer (via the transport). The consumer passes
     // it to ANativeWindow_queueBuffer, so SurfaceFlinger waits on it GPU-side before
diff --git a/src/compositor.cpp b/src/compositor.cpp
index a94ed81..08e7619 100644
--- a/src/compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/compositor.cpp
@@ -145,8 +145,13 @@ void Compositor::prePaintPass(RenderLayer *layer, QRegion *damage)
 {
     if (const QRegion repaints = layer->repaints(); !repaints.isEmpty()) {
         *damage += layer->mapToGlobal(repaints);
-        layer->resetRepaints();
     }
+    // This frame serves the layer's repaint request even when the layer has
+    // no region of its own: item repaints and frame requests are collected by
+    // its delegate below. Clearing the request only together with a region
+    // left it set on the scene layer forever, so every later frame request
+    // repainted the output with nothing new.
+    layer->resetRepaints();
 
     const QRegion repaints = layer->delegate()->prePaint();
     if (!repaints.isEmpty()) {
